# Adopt Jig as the canonical repository validator

Adopt Jig as the canonical repository validator.

## Acceptance criteria

- [x] Adopt Jig as the canonical repository validator.

## Dependencies

No explicit task dependency was recorded in the legacy TODO.

## Evidence

`.jig/jig.toml` is the tracked repository validation authority and configures
the external CSpell, Markdown, pytest, Ruff, nightly Clippy/rustfmt/tests,
stable
Rust check, and Jig-native repository-policy gates. `AGENTS.md` names
`jig validate --fail-fast --root .` as final validation evidence and explicitly
forbids substituting ad hoc formatter/compiler/linter/test runs.

The old `tools/vwj/` fallback duplicated only external gates while explicitly
admitting it did not evaluate Jig-native repository rules. It has been removed,
leaving no supported public validator that can be mistaken for canonical Jig
validation. Local Git hook projection is owned/refreshed by Jig integrations,
not by repository-authored fallback code.
